        - Output: If reduction is 'none', shape :math:`()`, :math:`(N)` or :math:`(N, d_1, d_2, ..., d_K)` with :math:`K \geq 1`
          in the case of K-dimensional loss, depending on the shape of the input. Otherwise, scalar.


        where:

        .. math::
            \begin{aligned}
                C ={} & \text{number of classes} \\
                N ={} & \text{batch size} \\
            \end{aligned}

